.TH "cbor::tag" 3 "Version 0.9.0" "mbedded-cbor" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
cbor::tag \- The tag number of a struct, in the member \fR\fBtag\fP\fP of its \fBcbor::describe_members\fP specialization\&.  

.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.PP
\fR#include <cbor/rfc8949\&.hpp>\fP
.SS "Public Attributes"

.in +1c
.ti -1c
.RI "std::uint64_t \fBnumber\fP"
.br
.in -1c
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
The tag number of a struct, in the member \fR\fBtag\fP\fP of its \fBcbor::describe_members\fP specialization\&. 

\fR\fBstructs as Packed CBOR, with fields at fixed offsets\fP\fP writes the number as the first item of each record of the struct\&. A read compares it, so a message of another struct gives \fRincorrect_type\fP\&. The tag of a record of a \fRstd::variant\fP member chooses a class alternative; a head of no alternative is \fRincorrect_type\fP\&. Each alternative has its own number, also when it derives from the class of another number\&. \fR\fBstructs\fP\fP takes the same description\&. These do not compile in \fR\fBstructs as Packed CBOR, with fields at fixed offsets\fP<T>\fP: a struct in \fRT\fP with no description or with \fRcbor::untagged\fP; two structs in \fRT\fP with one number, the alternatives of a variant included; a number of a standard type (0, 1, 2, 3, 24, 64 to 87, 100, 258, 1004 and 32873); a number that the IANA registry calls always invalid (21334, 65535, 4294967295 and 18446744073709551615)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
cbor::tag{number} → cbor::tag
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
